--- !u!114 &783559976
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 783559974}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<size=150%><b>How it works</b></size>\nAll of the math (parsing, evaluation,
    calculus and graph sampling) runs in Udon, VRChat's sandboxed scripting language.\n\n<b><color=#8fb8ff>1.
    Compile</color></b>\nEach expression is split into tokens, parsed into a syntax
    tree and classified: variable, function, curve, region, point, list, regression
    or table. It is then compiled to compact bytecode. Functions are inlined and
    definitions are ordered by what depends on what.\n\n<b><color=#8fb8ff>2. Evaluate</color></b>\nA
    small stack machine runs the bytecode on 256 points at once. Udon is slow per
    instruction, so working on whole arrays hides most of that cost. There are real
    and complex versions of every operation. Calculus is numerical: 5-point derivatives,
    Gauss\u2013Legendre integrals and direct sums.\n\n<b><color=#8fb8ff>3. Sample</color></b>\nCurves
    start with evenly spaced points, then add more where the curve bends or gets
    steep, and break the line at asymptotes. Implicit equations like x\xB2 + y\xB2
    = 9 are sampled on a grid and turned into a distance field stored in a texture.\n\n<b><color=#8fb8ff>4.
    Draw</color></b>\nUdon builds meshes for lines, shaded regions and points. Tiny
    shaders only draw them: smooth lines, dashes for < and >, shading, and the zero-contour
    of the distance texture. Panning moves the existing meshes instantly while new
    samples are computed in the background.\n\n<b><color=#8fb8ff>5. Stay smooth</color></b>\nWork
    is time-sliced: only a few milliseconds per frame, so the frame rate stays steady
    and graphs sharpen over a moment. Quest uses smaller budgets and fewer samples.\n\n<b><color=#8fb8ff>6.
    Sync</color></b>\nOnly the expression text, slider ranges, view and settings
    travel over the network. Every player computes the graphs locally, and animated
    sliders follow the shared server clock so they stay in step."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
